Title: Add coverage gate to make test plus coverage dev dependency
Created: 2026-05-28
Author: Claude

--- log ---
2026-05-28T17:42Z Claude created — surfaced during test-coverage analysis (branch claude/test-coverage-analysis-OwuVY)

--- body ---
## Context

Current fast-suite line coverage is **68%**. There is no coverage gate,
so coverage can silently regress, and `coverage`/`pytest-cov` is not a
declared dev dependency (the analysis had to run `uv run --with coverage`).

## Approach

- Add `pytest-cov` (or `coverage`) to the `dev` dependency group in
  `pyproject.toml`.
- Add `--cov=src/aedist --cov-fail-under=65` to `make test` (not
  `test-fast`, to keep the dev loop quick), or a dedicated `make coverage`
  target. Start the floor slightly below current (65%) and ratchet up as
  0379/0380/0381 land.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `coverage`/`pytest-cov` in `[dependency-groups] dev`.
- [ ] `make test` (or `make coverage`) fails when coverage drops below floor.
- [ ] Floor documented; ratchet plan noted.

## Blocked-by ordering

Best landed after 0379/0380 raise the baseline, so the floor can be set
meaningfully. Not strictly blocking.
